DASH.todo={title:"What to do as a normal investor",note:"General info, not personal financial advice.",
l:["<b>Don't buy the AI dip blindly.</b> Alphabet, Amazon and Intel all fell hard on spending and cash-flow worries; keep regular investing (DCA) in broad funds instead of loading up on the fallen names.",
"<b>Diversification is doing its job.</b> Most stocks rose Thursday while big tech fell; an equal-weight or broad index fund spreads the AI risk.",
"<b>Rates are still high.</b> Inflation (PCE 3.6%) is hot and a December hike is still likely (about 78-85%); avoid new high-interest debt and lock in fixed rates where you can.",
"<b>Cash and short-term bonds still pay.</b> Short-term deposits and bonds are a fine place to wait while tech reprices.",
"<b>Oil risk hasn't gone away.</b> Talk of talks pulled oil back, but strike options after the 3 Nov midterms are on the table; budget for higher fuel.",
"<b>Gold is a hedge, not a bet.</b> It is sitting near $4,000; keep only a small slice.",
"<b>Keep crypto small.</b> BTC broke below ~$78k support after a suspected Binance hack; expect more swings.",
"<b>Thai investors: be patient and selective.</b> The SET fell 1.37% to 1,544.60 as foreigners sold ฿2.9B, near the 1,540 support. In our dividend table, SPALI, ICHI, AP, TVO and PTT trade at or below their buy zones (green); check earnings and payout safety first."]};
// Glossary: m = regex matched against an element's text (li/td/h2); d = plain explanation + what it means now.
DASH.glossary={
fg:{m:"Fear & Greed",d:"CNN's 0-100 mood gauge for US stocks, built from 7 signals. 34.6 = Fear (after Thursday's close), down a touch from 35.9 but well above 20.0 a week ago. Investors fled big tech, and Amazon's and Intel's after-hours drops may weigh today."},
fgbands:{d:"0-25 Extreme Fear, 26-45 Fear, 46-55 Neutral, 56-75 Greed, 76-100 Extreme Greed. Fear often comes before rebounds, but not always."},
nk:{m:"Nuclear Escalation",d:"Our editorial 0-100 tension score from weighted news factors. Not a probability. ~46 = Elevated, up about 1 point: Trump was briefed on Iran strike options and the Houthis claim more hits on Saudi oil sites, though Vance opened a new letter channel to Tehran."},
nkbands:{d:"0-20 Low, 21-40 Guarded, 41-60 Elevated, 61-80 High, 81-100 Severe. Each factor's score × weight adds up to the total."},
mom:{m:"Market momentum",d:"S&P 500 vs its 125-day average. 35.4 = fear: Thursday's drop in big tech pulled the index back toward its trend."},
str:{m:"price strength",d:"Stocks at 52-week highs vs lows. 32.0 = more lows than highs, fear (62 NYSE highs vs 120 lows Thursday)."},
brd:{m:"breadth",d:"Volume in rising vs falling stocks. 35.4 = fear, but improving: most stocks rose Thursday even as big tech fell."},
pc:{m:"Put/Call",d:"Compares bets on stocks falling vs rising. 29.8 = lots of protection buying, a fearful sign."},
vix:{m:"VIX",d:"The market's 'fear gauge' of expected S&P swings. Reading 50.0 = neutral (VIX about 17); the selloff stayed contained to tech."},
sh:{m:"Safe-haven",d:"Stock returns vs bonds lately. 9.6 = extreme fear: bonds rallied Thursday as money left tech."},
jb:{m:"Junk bond",d:"Extra yield on risky company debt. 50.0 = neutral: lenders are not panicking."},
f1:{m:"Active wars",d:"Wars that could pull in nuclear powers. Scored 66 (up from 65): CENTCOM briefed Trump on Iran strike options for after the midterms, while Vance wrote to Tehran to restart talks. Iran isn't a confirmed nuclear state."},
f2:{m:"Russia-Ukraine",d:"A nuclear power at war. Scored 39 (up from 37), the biggest weight: a deadly strike on Dnipro's train station and a big Ukrainian drone attack toward Moscow; the Kremlin ties talks to the battlefield."},
f3:{m:"spillover",d:"Risk the Mideast war widens. Scored 72 (up from 69): the Houthis claim hits on three Saudi oil sites (unconfirmed) and Iran says three tankers hit mines near Hormuz."},
f4:{m:"diplomacy channels",d:"Are big powers talking? Higher = fewer working channels. Scored 24 (down from 26): Vance's letter to Iran's security chief is a new direct channel."},
f5:{m:"Arms-control",d:"Nuclear threats and treaty news. Scored 25 (unchanged): no explicit nuclear threats; Vance urged Iran to negotiate on its nuclear program."},
sp:{m:"S&P",d:"500 big US companies, the main US stock benchmark. ~7,720 Thursday (−0.31%), its first drop in four days, led by Alphabet; most members actually rose."},
dow:{m:"Dow",d:"30 large 'blue-chip' US stocks, more old-economy. −0.25% Thursday."},
ndq:{m:"Nasdaq",d:"Tech-heavy US index. −1.38% Thursday on Alphabet's record drop; futures fell about 1.6% more after Amazon and Intel results."},
y10:{m:"10Y",d:"Yield on 10-year US government bonds, which drives loan rates. ~4.99% (Thursday): just under 5% as bonds rallied on the tech selloff."},
wti:{m:"WTI",d:"US crude oil price. ~$102.0 settle Thursday (−0.8%), eased on renewed US-Iran outreach but still above $100."},
brent:{m:"Brent",d:"Global benchmark crude. ~$114.9 (December contract, −0.4% Thursday), near a six-month high."},
dsl:{m:"diesel",d:"US average diesel price. ~$6.35/gal (AAA, 28 Oct, latest we found), just under the 22 Sep record of $6.53; diesel futures fell 1.6% Thursday."},
gold:{m:"^Gold$|Gold and|gold slice",d:"Classic safe haven. ~$4,009: lower as hot PCE inflation kept December hike bets alive; $4,000 is the line."},
btc:{m:"Bitcoin|BTC",d:"The largest crypto. ~$77.8k = bearish: it fell through ~$78k support after a suspected Binance hack and the tech selloff."},
bull:{d:"BULLISH = we expect it to rise or hold strong. MILDLY = a leaning, not a strong view."},
neu:{d:"NEUTRAL = no clear direction; it could go either way."},
bear:{d:"BEARISH = we expect it to fall or stay weak."},
ff:{m:"Fed funds",d:"The Fed's key short-term interest rate. 3.75-4.00%, held on 28 Oct with two officials wanting a hike; next decision 9 Dec."},
cpi:{m:"CPI",d:"Consumer price inflation. 3.7% YoY is well above the Fed's 2% goal; the Fed's preferred PCE gauge was 3.6% in September."},
ppi:{m:"PPI",d:"Prices businesses pay, an early inflation signal. +6.3% in a year, the biggest since 2022."},
odds:{m:"Hike odds|Fed odds",d:"Market-implied chance of a Fed hike (fed funds futures, CME FedWatch). About 78-85% for a quarter-point hike on 9 Dec, a little lower after Thursday's bond rally."},
dxy:{m:"Dollar index",d:"DXY: the dollar against 6 major currencies. About 101.9 Thursday, down 0.15% (DTN)."},
jpy:{m:"USD/JPY|Yen",d:"Yen per dollar. ~157.7 = a weak yen; the BOJ decides today and is expected to hold at 1.25%."},
cds:{m:"CDS",d:"Credit default swap: insurance against a company defaulting. CoreWeave's CDS went past 11% (a distress level) and Meta's hit a record in October as AI spending strained cash flow."},
bot:{m:"BOT policy|BoT meeting|BOT MPC|BoT decision|BoT held|BoT kept",d:"Bank of Thailand's key rate. Held at 1.00% on 28 Oct in a unanimous vote (fourth hold in a row); the BoT sees 2026 inflation at 2.1% and is watching oil and El Niño risks."},
set:{m:"SET",d:"SET = Thai stock index; SET50 = its 50 biggest stocks. SET 1,544.60 (−1.37% Thu 29 Oct), dragged by DELTA and energy; 1,540 is the next support."},
flow:{m:"Foreign flows|foreigners",d:"Net buying minus selling by foreign investors. −฿2.86B on 29 Oct, a second day of selling; October to date −฿7.66B, year to date +฿17.45B (SET data)."},
dca:{m:"DCA",d:"Dollar-cost averaging: invest a fixed amount on a schedule regardless of price, which smooths out bad timing."}};
